  |t| >= 2.776 would be needed for significance at p<0.05; this is 0.97

  VERDICT: tuning does not measurably help.
  The paired difference is within one standard error of zero, so the two
  configurations are indistinguishable on this data. Note that the sign of
  the difference flipped between the 30% run (-0.0003) and the full-data run
  (+0.0024): a real effect should not change sign when you simply add data.
  The hand-set baseline is what serves.

